-- The Ace Tsar Molotov hookah (catalogue p26) shows the shop's own photos (Google Drive, 2026-11-27), not applied live yet.
-- The shop's green and blue Tsar (IMG_0684, IMG_0685) stood on a patterned mat that showed through their clear glass base;
-- store/tools/catalog/clear_glass.py clears what is seen through the glass and keeps the glass's own outline and highlights.
--   OSS-100084 (green chip): shop/ace-tsar-molotov-green, its own photo (it showed the blue catalogue photo, "Shown in blue").
--   OSS-100081 (blue chip): shop/ace-tsar-molotov-blue in place of the enlarged catalogue photo ("Photo to be upscaled" goes).
--   OSS-100080, OSS-100083 (red and yellow chips, no photo of their own): still "Shown in blue", now with the shop's blue photo.
-- Each colour's chip is measured from its shop photo (photo_hex, photos.colour_of), as for the catalogue photos.
-- Each line is the Ace seed's own UPDATE for that one item (catalog.py seed --supplier ace), so only its supplier columns
-- move and a second run touches no row. Needs store/public/img/pc/shop/ace-tsar-molotov-{green,blue}*.webp deployed with
-- the same commit. Run after shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql.
